  "notes": "BrasilAgro (Companhia Brasileira de Propriedades Agrícolas) B3-listed since 2006; Cresud subsidiary. BRL reporting. JULY-JUNE FISCAL YEAR — fiscal quarters are 1T (Jul-Sep), 2T (Oct-Dec), 3T (Jan-Mar), 4T (Apr-Jun). FY references such as 'FY24' = ano-safra 2023/24 ending Jun-2024. Five operating segments: Soja (soybeans), Cana-de-açúcar (sugarcane), Algodão (cotton), Pecuária (cattle), and Imobiliário (real-estate transactions = farm sales — lumpy, can dominate any given quarter). IFRS reporter (CVM): owned farms carried at fair value via biological assets + property revaluation, so propertyFmvMM moves quarterly. Annual independent appraisal (typically Deloitte) underpins fair-value carrying amount. Quarterly data from CVM ITR/DFP filings + ri.brasil-agro.com release decks. grossRevenueMM = receita bruta, revenueMM = receita líquida (pre-PIS/COFINS deductions ~9.25%). Land Transformation business model: BrasilAgro acquires undeveloped/cerrado land cheap, develops it (cattle → cropping rotation), and sells parcels at significant FV uplift. Hectare-to-acre: 1 ha = 2.47105 acres; portfolio of ~330k acres includes both owned + leased. FY 2006/07 — FY 2019/20 backfill from CVM RAD filings (DFPs) — annual only as quarterly archives are sparse pre-2020 and segment splits weren't always disclosed. IPO May-2006 raised R$583M. Operations ramped slowly: from 4 farms / ~80k ha in 2007 to ~200k ha owned by FY15. Soja/Cana/Pecuária established as core segments; Algodão added 2011/12.",
